{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Paper Game Prototype.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Paper Game Prototype.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"paper game prototype paper game prototype","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Paper Game Prototype.md","fileName":"Paper Game Prototype.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Paper Game Prototype","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:27\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Prototyping Strategy]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Prototyping Strategy","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Paper Game Prototype.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Paper Game Prototype.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"paper game prototype paper game prototype","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Paper Game Prototype.md","fileName":"Paper Game Prototype.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Paper Game Prototype","heading":"Paper Game Prototype","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A paper game prototype represents screens, objects, rules, and state changes with inexpensive physical materials. A facilitator can perform operations that software would eventually automate, allowing interaction ideas to be tested before code exists.\n\nPaper is especially useful for clarifying the player's role, the information that must be visible, and how objects relate in the playspace. It is less suitable when timing, continuous motion, or sensory response is the central question.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Prototyping Strategy","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Paper Game Prototype.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Paper Game Prototype.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"paper game prototype paper game prototype","